Rem -->COPRINUS SUBSECTION ATRAMENTARII
Rem -->Pileus medium-sized, 30-80 x 20-60 mm, ochre-brown, grey-brown or grey, squamulose only at centre, often seemingly smooth. Growing fasciculate, on wood, trunks or wood-chips. Spores < 10 µm long when smooth, if larger then spores warty (subsect. Atramentarii (Fr.) Konr. & Maubl.).
1,0 $ Pileus c. 20-30 mm high, ochraceous, almost smooth; spore breadth 4.5-5.2 µm: $ C. acuminatus
1,2 $ . Pileus usually larger, orange-brown, grey-brown or grey; spore breadth 5-6 µm
2,0 $ Pileus grey-brown or grey, veil scarce, adpressed, only at centre: $ C. atramentarius
2,0 $ Pileus orange-brown, veil more abundant, squamulose, often with reflexed tips: $ C. romagnesianus
3,0$Pileus medium-sized, 30-80 x 20-60 mm, ochre-brown, grey-brown or grey, squamulose only at centre, often seemingly smooth. Growing fasciculate, on wood, trunks or wood-chips. Spores < 10 µm long when smooth, if larger then spores warty (subsect. Atramentarii (Fr.) Konr. & Maubl.)$ATRAMENTARII